                "Modified [`onSubmit()` to pass an `onSuccess` callback to `saveProfile()`](code:src/routes/account/components/ProfileForm.tsx#L14-16), which calls `reset()` with the profile the server returned."
              ],
              "waypoints": [
                {
                  "id": "w1",
                  "title": "Modified `<ProfileForm />` to reset the form to the saved profile",
                  "declaration": "ProfileForm",
                  "reading": "The author modified a component `ProfileForm` that now calls `reset()` with the saved profile when a save succeeds. `onSubmit()` passes `{ onSuccess }` to `saveProfile()`, and the `mutate` function of [`useUpdateProfile()`](code:src/hooks/use-profile.ts#L10-18) calls that callback with the profile that `updateProfile()` in `src/api/profile.ts` returned. `reset()` writes that name and email to the two inputs and makes them the default values of the form, so that the form compares a later edit with the saved profile and not with the `profile` that [`<AccountPage />` passed](code:src/routes/account/index.tsx#L10) on the first render. A save that fails does not call `onSuccess`, so the inputs keep the text the user typed.",
